Job submissions per project

run_estimation.sh commands per project, run from segmentation/ on the cluster.
They call sbatch for the project and activate the env (segamega,
PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1) for the jobs. The last column's command (--segment)
submits both steps at once: the segmentation job waits for the pose job to end
(sbatch --dependency=afterany) and then segments whatever pose files exist. To
resubmit only a segmentation job, use --segment-only with the --seg-* options.

Estimates are from ../time_estimation.md, based on the SRT-2-Modellvideos and
SRT-1-Modellvideos test runs combined: pose estimation takes about 0.84 s per
second of video with 8 CPUs (0.53 and 0.95 in the two runs), segmentation about
6.1 s per file (8.5 and 5.3). Requested times are about 2x the estimate,
with a minimum of 1 hour. Jobs that run out of time can simply be resubmitted:
finished files are skipped. Estimates are in hours:minutes.


Pose estimation uses 8 CPUs (also used as --workers), segmentation 2 CPUs.
Projects with long files (SMILE2, SMILE, SRT-2, SMILE_2018, Noah David: about
15-60 minutes per file) get more memory and time for segmentation, because the
model attends over the whole video and long files haven't been tested yet. Run
one long SMILE2 file first and adjust.

